  "businessReality": "fictional",
  "description": "The asset specification for the Ardwell & Roe visual-ceiling benchmark. This is a PLAN, not an inventory: `bytes: absent` means the file does not exist yet. Nothing here claims an asset the factory holds. The floor below is what a run must satisfy before it may be called an ideal-input baseline, and tooling/lib/benchmark-asset-readiness.mjs is what enforces it.",
  "providerNeutral": "No image provider is named in this corpus, and a test enforces it over every file in this directory. The requirement is governed synthetic bytes with explicit provenance and publication permission; where they are produced is not the factory's business, and switching source must never require a code change. Provider candidates for a benchmark that has not been earned are recorded separately in config/capability-providers.json and are not part of this plan's contract.",
  "floor": {
    "requiredAssetsPresent": "all",
    "minimumProjectsWithPrimary": 4,
    "minimumProjectAssets": 8,
    "minimumPortraits": 2,
    "brandAssetRequired": true,
    "heroCapableRequired": true,
    "rationale": "Four projects with a primary frame is the point at which a work index reads as a portfolio rather than a sample; eight project assets is enough for at least one project to carry a sequence. Two portraits covers the founders, which is what a studio page is actually about. These thresholds come from the source pack — six projects, five people — and are deliberately below its full extent, because the floor is the point at which asset scarcity stops being the confound, not the point of perfection."
  },
